  "notes": "West leads the ♥K against 7♠. West's opening heart lead is won by South with the ♥A. Most of the time South will be able to ruff his ♦2 in dummy and easily take all 13 tricks. South should begin by leading a spade to dummy's ♠A.\n\nWest's discard means that the ♠2 cannot be used to ruff the ♦2. It must be used to pick up East's ♠J. The remaining trumps should be drawn, finessing on the second round.\n\nIf clubs are 3-3, dummy's fourth club will provide a discard for the ♦2. If East has 4 or more clubs, the contract has no hope. If West has 4 or more clubs along with the ♥Q that he is marked with from the lead, he can be squeezed on the run of South's spade and diamond winners.\n\nWhen the ♦A is cashed, West is squeezed. A heart discard will set up dummy's ♥J while a club discard will establish the fourth round of clubs in dummy. The ♥J is discarded from dummy unless the ♥Q appears first.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥K against 7♠. West's opening heart lead is won by South with the ♥A. Most of the time South will be able to ruff his ♦2 in dummy and easily take all 13 tricks. South should begin by leading a spade to dummy's ♠A.",
    "West's discard means that the ♠2 cannot be used to ruff the ♦2. It must be used to pick up East's ♠J. The remaining trumps should be drawn, finessing on the second round.",
